# Implementation Plan - HOTFIX-011 — Global Keyboard Shortcut to Restore BatmanOverlay Focus

Implement a native Windows global hotkey (`Ctrl + E`) using `RegisterHotKey` to restore and activate keyboard focus to BatmanOverlay from any application or transparency level, without modifying opacity or window state settings.

## Proposed Changes

### Platform Layer

#### [NEW] [global_hotkey.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/platform/global_hotkey.py)
- Create `WindowsGlobalHotkeyManager` wrapping native `user32.RegisterHotKey` and `user32.UnregisterHotKey`.
- Define constants: `MOD_CONTROL = 0x0002`, `VK_E = 0x45`, `WM_HOTKEY = 0x0312`, `HOTKEY_ID_CTRL_E = 0x011B`.
- Log success/failure gracefully without crashing if `Ctrl+E` is already registered by another process.

---

### UI & Main Window Layer

#### [MODIFY] [overlay_visibility_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/overlay_visibility_panel.py)
- Update hint label to: `"Shortcuts: Ctrl+Q decrease opacity · Ctrl+W increase opacity · Ctrl+E focus"`.

#### [MODIFY] [main_window.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/main_window.py)
- Register `Ctrl+E` global hotkey on startup using `WindowsGlobalHotkeyManager`.
- Override `nativeEvent(self, event_type, message)`:
  - Intercept `WM_HOTKEY` (`0x0312`) when `wParam == HOTKEY_ID_CTRL_E`.
  - Invoke `restore_and_focus()`.
- Implement `restore_and_focus()`:
  - Restores window if minimized (`showNormal()` / `ShowWindow`).
  - Brings `MainWindow` to front (`show()`, `raise_()`, `activateWindow()`, `SetForegroundWindow`, `setFocus()`).
  - Preserves current opacity/transparency levels and all settings intact.
- Unregister `Ctrl+E` hotkey in `closeEvent` and app shutdown.

